{%- doc -%}
  The card a mega menu panel carries at its right edge: a picture on white, a
  title, a line of copy and one button (Figma: Collection Card 3, 491:14001).

  It is 255px wide and holds that width — the panel places it against the page
  margin, and a card that grew with the panel would leave the link columns to
  take up the slack. Its height is the panel's: the picture is the flexible part,
  so the file's two heights (288 beside one column, 312 beside two) both fall out
  of the same card rather than needing a variant.

  The picture sits on white and is fitted rather than cropped. The photographs
  this takes are trays shot wide on a white sweep, so `cover` would cut the ends
  off the tray; `contain` keeps the whole object and lets the white it already
  has meet the white behind it.

  @param {object} [image] - The picture. Renders an empty white panel when absent.
  @param {string} [heading] - The card's title, in the display face.
  @param {string} [text] - One line under the title.
  @param {string} [button_label] - The button's text. No label, no button.
  @param {string} [button_link] - Where the button goes.
  @param {string} [class] - Additional CSS classes.

  @example
  {% render 'ui-mega-promo',
    image: block.settings.image,
    heading: 'Choose Your Own Treat',
    text: 'Design your box',
    button_label: 'Shop now',
    button_link: '/collections/choose-your-own-treat'
  %}
{%- enddoc -%}

<div class="ui-mega-promo {{ class }}">
  {%- if image != blank -%}
    <div class="ui-mega-promo__media">
      {{
        image
        | image_url: width: 446
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'lazy',
          class: 'ui-mega-promo__image',
          widths: '223, 446',
          sizes: '223px',
          alt: image.alt | default: heading
      }}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if heading != blank or text != blank -%}
    <div class="ui-mega-promo__body">
      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        <p class="ui-mega-promo__heading">{{ heading }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if text != blank -%}
        <p class="ui-mega-promo__text">{{ text }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if button_label != blank -%}
    {% render 'ui-button',
      variant: 'primary',
      label: button_label,
      link: button_link,
      full_width: true,
      class: 'ui-mega-promo__button'
    %}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .ui-mega-promo {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    inline-size: 255px;
    padding: 16px;
    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--ui-color-light-blue);
  }

  /*
   * The picture keeps the box the file draws — 223 by 162 inside a 255 card —
   * rather than taking its height from the photograph. Collection images are
   * square as often as not, and a box that sized itself to one would make the
   * card 60px taller than the panel it sits in.
   */
  .ui-mega-promo__media {
    display: flex;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    aspect-ratio: 223 / 162;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background-color: var(--ui-color-white);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ui-mega-promo__image {
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .ui-mega-promo__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .ui-mega-promo__heading {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--ui-color-black);
  }

  .ui-mega-promo__text {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--ui-font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: var(--ui-font-body-weight);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--ui-color-gray);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
